  <p>As well as being sweet, peach schnapps cocktails tend to be very refreshing, and a lot of them strike me as summer drinks. Sound good? Let’s get mixing!</p>

  <h2>What is peach schnapps?</h2>
  <p>We go into <a href="/what-is-peach-schnapps/">more detail about what peach schnapps is here</a>, but essentially it’s a peach version of the popular schnapps.</p>

  <h3>So, what’s schnapps?</h3>
  <p><em>Schnapps</em> is a German word for any kind of strong alcoholic drink, and over the years it’s become known as a style of drink. It can take several forms:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Distilled fruit brandy.</li>
    <li>Herbal liqueurs.</li>
    <li>Infusions, where flavour is extracted from plants using a solvent such as water, oil or, in the case of schnapps, alcohol.</li>
    <li>Flavoured liqueurs. This is where peach schnapps comes in.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Classic peach schnapps cocktails</h2>
  <p>Peach schnapps is a key ingredient in a few modern classics that you’ll want to make and drink right away. These include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/cocktails/woo-woo/">Woo Woo</a>, a refreshing mix of vodka, peach schnapps and cranberry juice that’s entirely too drinkable.</li>
    <li><a href="/cocktails/sex-on-the-beach/">Sex on the Beach</a>, a classic holiday cocktail that mixes vodka, peach schnapps, orange juice and cranberry juice for a sweet thirst-quencher.</li>
    <li><a href="/cocktails/sex-in-the-driveway/">Sex in the Driveway</a>, a boozy yet refreshing drink that mixes vodka, peach schnapps, blue curaçao and Sprite.</li>
    <li><a href="/cocktails/fuzzy-navel/">Fuzzy Navel</a>, a staple drink of my youth that mixes peach schnapps with orange juice for something simple yet refreshing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What peach schnapps should I use?</h2>
  <p>Use whatever peach schnapps you have in the house, or prefer, for these cocktails. But if you’re on the hunt for a new bottle, we recommend Archers.</p>

